course: dictionary
lesson: 14265
title: Nightie and bedtime words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nightie is a nightdress, a loose dress that you wear in bed. You can work out what a word means from the words around it. «Mum helped Lily find her nightie, and then she climbed into bed.» The clues are bed and climbed into bed: a nightie is something you wear at bedtime.
explain: Nightie is an informal word, so you will hear it at home, at sleepovers and in stories. «Ava packed her toothbrush and her nightie for the sleepover.» The clues are packed and sleepover, which tell you the nightie is for sleeping in.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Ava packed her toothbrush and her nightdress for the sleepover» still makes sense, so nightie means nightdress.
fact: A nightie is a nightdress: a loose dress worn in bed.
fact: Nightie is an informal word, used in everyday speech.
fact: Nighties are mostly worn by girls and women.
fact: The plural of nightie is nighties.
fact: «In her nightie» in a story often means she has just got out of bed.
exercise: «Lily put on her nightie and climbed into bed.» What is a nightie? | A school bag | *A loose dress worn in bed | A kind of hat for the snow | A pair of warm socks
exercise: Which word is an informal word for a nightdress? | bedside | blanket | pillowcase | *nightie
exercise: «Ella was in her nightie when the doorbell rang, so she had just got out of bed.» What does being in her nightie tell you? | *She was wearing her nightdress | She was wearing her school uniform | She was swimming in the sea | She was going to the shops
test: «Ava packed her toothbrush and her nightie for the sleepover.» What does nightie mean? | A game played at a party | A sort of toothbrush | A kind of school bag | *A nightdress, a loose dress worn in bed
test: Which is the plural of nightie? | *nighties | nightieses | nightys | nightie's
exam: Which sentence uses nightie correctly? | «The nightie was a sum with ten numbers.» | *«Put your nightie on, it's time for bed.» | «The nightie was an ancient castle on the hill.» | «The nightie was loud and ran very fast.»
